      {
        "id": "s1b",
        "kind": "explain",
        "title": "Drawing the line",
        "body": "To draw a line from its equation, pick three $x$ values, work out $y$ for each, plot the points, and join them with a ruler. The third point is a check: if it is off the line, one of the three is wrong.\n\nFor $y = 2x - 3$: $x = 0$ gives $y = -3$, $x = 1$ gives $y = -1$, and $x = 3$ gives $y = 3$.",
